1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:01,806
Old windows aren't melting.

2
00:00:02,306 --> 00:00:06,872
Some old panes are thicker at the bottom, so people say glass flows.

3
00:00:07,372 --> 00:00:12,774
But at room temperature, glass would take far longer than the age of the universe to sag.

4
00:00:13,274 --> 00:00:17,453
Old glass was spun or blown by hand, so it came out uneven.

5
00:00:17,753 --> 00:00:20,041
Builders often set the thick edge down.

6
00:00:20,541 --> 00:00:22,852
It was uneven from the day it was made.
